+## Ranked follow-ups: expected gain, effort, exactness risk
+
+1. Copy suppression (implemented): small/content-dependent expected decode gain, potentially zero or negative;
+   very small port using existing gates; low policy risk, but full-model token equality still required because
+   different verified row shapes can expose a pre-existing kernel inconsistency. Best cheap A/B, not113tok/s fix.
+2. Instrument actual verified/head/copy rows, round time and acceptance, then compare existing joint0 vs joint1
+   settings independently: no new scheduler, low engineering effort and highest diagnostic value. Concurrency
+   benefit unmeasured; solo throughput gain is not implied. Never bundle this setting into the no-copy A/B.
+3. Audit native collective eligibility at exact Markov/Engram/logit byte counts: low-to-medium investigation,
+   possible small gain only if an actual fallback is found. We already call comm.allGather for Engram
+   (forward_engram.zig:36/53), logits (forward_graph.zig:23; forward_glue.zig:139), and sampled-pair selection
+   (forward_sample.zig:54/97), and actual both-rail usage is proven. Do not port a new ring speculatively.
+   Pure-copy routing can be exact, but rank-order/side-stream/fallback contracts make a new collective a bigger port.
+4. Kernel crossover/profile work: potentially meaningful C3/C4 gains, high effort and exactness risk. Inspect
+   actual dense kernel variants and graph-bucket padding first: rowtab.zig:5 has1..8/12/16/24/32/48/64 buckets.
+   HeNryous's >16-row fallback is specific to its plugin. Their0042b/0046/0050 alter reduction/precision paths;
+   require independent per-projection references and equality gates, not a flag rename or copied benchmark claim.
+5. Graph-cache caps: memory/lifetime benefit, no expected positive peak decode gain, medium effort. Mia cap3
+   was slower; cap128 was level. Separate bounded-ownership proposal if our caches demonstrably grow.
+6. Pack change: potentially large but unquantified throughput/acceptance change; high quality/exactness cost.
+   New pack must have independent KL/top-token quality panels, all assets and model gates. Outside cheap ports.
+7. Indexer TP query-row sharding: demonstrated prefill gains, no isolated decode gain; separate prefill proposal,
+   preserve each original row's arithmetic and all rank contracts. Not a solution to this solo short-decode gap.
+
