+## HeNryous: exactly what v5's 5/5/4/4 does
+
+Primary reports: NVIDIA [post 3, v4i](https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/t/386295/3) and
+[post 5, v5](https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/t/386295/5). Direct public topic JSON returned all 17 posts;
+the web-reader endpoint failed, but direct HTTPS JSON retrieval succeeded. Source was checked independently below.
+
+There are THREE decisions, not one adaptive 5/5/4/4 algorithm:
+
+1. **Concurrency schedule, patch 0040, configuration only.** The
+   [historical v5 launcher](https://github.com/HeNryous/deepseek-v41-1017-dgx-spark/blob/4ead449c7a8ec2998fc232eee71efa0e58facec6/serve/serve_example.sh#L21)
+   passes `num_speculative_tokens=5` and `num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size=[[1,2,5],[3,4,4]]`.
+   Existing vLLM dynamic speculation looks up k by the scheduled batch's request count. C1/C2 use k5,
+   C3/C4 k4: target windows are respectively 6/12/15/20 rows INCLUDING the pending/bonus row per request.
+   This is not a confidence or acceptance controller. Variant A (5/5/4/3) stayed <=16 rows but lost C4 code.
+2. **Next-step window adaptation, patch 0047 v2.**
+   [Actual patch](https://github.com/HeNryous/deepseek-v41-1017-dgx-spark/blob/382071728ce69700b28e7a5ea197ab0a48b2232c/patches/0047-dsv41-adaptive-verify-window.patch).
+   Scheduler computes accepted drafts as `max(len(generated_token_ids)-num_sampled,0)`. For a non-stale result,
+   observation x is accepted drafts plus one if every offered draft was accepted (censored acceptance needs room
+   to expand). First observation initializes the request EMA; later EMA = 0.7*old + 0.3*x by default.
+   For the next scheduled step, start want at K_MIN; take the MAXIMUM across requests of ceil(EMA+margin), bounded
+   by the concurrency schedule's cap. If ANY request has no history, is a prefill chunk, or EMA>=HI, return the
+   full cap immediately. This returns ONE batch-wide k, not independent target window widths per request.
+   Launcher values: min2, margin1.0, HI1.6, max requests4; code defaults differ: margin1.5, HI99, max requests2,
+   alpha0.3, adaptive disabled. Requires a dynamic schedule; without one the call site does not adapt.
+   Graph setup captures the extra k+sampled-row widths, limited to the configured eligible batch sizes.
+   Checked current overlaid [scheduler.py](https://github.com/HeNryous/deepseek-v41-1017-dgx-spark/blob/382071728ce69700b28e7a5ea197ab0a48b2232c/docker/files/vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py#L2123)
+   and [cudagraph_utils.py](https://github.com/HeNryous/deepseek-v41-1017-dgx-spark/blob/382071728ce69700b28e7a5ea197ab0a48b2232c/docker/files/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py#L305), not just prose.
+3. **Current-round confidence depth.** The device depth policy decides how many offered drafts may be accepted;
+   the stock `conf` objective divides expected tokens by table verify+draft milliseconds. In this stack, rows
+   past that depth skip routed experts but still incur dense/attention/indexer/mHC work inside the scheduled
+   window. Therefore shallower confidence depth alone does not remove the whole target-row cost.
+   [depth_policy.py](https://github.com/HeNryous/deepseek-v41-1017-dgx-spark/blob/382071728ce69700b28e7a5ea197ab0a48b2232c/docker/files/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/depth_policy.py#L190).
+
+**Current correction:** [0040 documentation](https://github.com/HeNryous/deepseek-v41-1017-dgx-spark/blob/382071728ce69700b28e7a5ea197ab0a48b2232c/patches/0040-dsv41-dynamic-sd-config.md)
+records switching on Oct 21 to k5 at C1–C4 after widening the dense kernel and adding adaptation: reported
+geometric-mean +1.27% versus 5/5/4/4, C4 code +2.6%, JSON +5.2%, prose +0.7%, T0 texts equal.
+The [current launcher](https://github.com/HeNryous/deepseek-v41-1017-dgx-spark/blob/382071728ce69700b28e7a5ea197ab0a48b2232c/serve/serve_example.sh#L25)
+uses `[[1,4,5],[5,8,3]]`, adapting only <=4-request steps, and still names image v24. Current README describes
+later v30/v32 experiments; do not silently equate README's latest image discussion with the launcher's selected image.
+
+**Local transfer:** `draft/lanes.zig:111` attaches the family's row policy; core `windows.zig:240` dispatches to
+that trim before the generic allocator. `draft/policy.zig` chooses per-window depths, and `windows.zig:301`
