+  replaces 0042. Previously >16 rows fell back from plugin `exl3_mrow` to exllamav3 plus casts. New ring kernel
+  transforms input in 128-column blocks into two 32x128 shared stages, reducing K5 shared memory to about 27KB
+  and enabling two blocks/SM; restores finer k-slicing. Default switch still limits mrow to16; launcher opts into32
+  and ring from9 rows. Reported dense-only 18/24-row time falls to13.2/13.7ms; C3/C4 code +5.0/+7.7% for ring
+  from9. Deterministic slice order differs from prior kernel; changed T0 texts are admitted. This is not a safe
+  drop-in bit-preserving port and not proof this engine has the same >16 fallback. This engine's own emit/kernel/asset path must be traced.
+- **HeNryous 0045, collective coverage:**
+  [patches/0045-dsv41-exl3-rdma-allgather.patch](https://github.com/HeNryous/deepseek-v41-1017-dgx-spark/blob/382071728ce69700b28e7a5ea197ab0a48b2232c/patches/0045-dsv41-exl3-rdma-allgather.patch)
+  adds all-gather to a plugin ring that previously handled all-reduce only: Markov value/index pairs, Engram
+  rows, logits. Shared sequence/slots across gathers/reduces require identical rank order and no side-stream
+  issue of redirected gathers. Output layout is [outer,rank,inner], pure copies; 4-byte units cover 8-byte Markov
+  pairs, 16-byte units when aligned. Shape/dtype/dim choose route; misalignment is handled locally; setup fallback
+  is collective. Limits keep large prompt/vision operations on NCCL. Launcher AG limit3072KiB covers 24-row
+  BF16 vocab-half logits (3,102,720 bytes); default256KiB does not. One comment says3200, but actual configured
+ 3072KiB exceeds this shape's exact byte count. Larger rings cost pinned host memory. With0046, reported C1 +1.6%.
+- **HeNryous 0046, head crossover:**
