+Potential later work: record exact shapes/bytes/routing of Markov/Engram/logit exchanges and physical graph buckets;
+small routing/crossover adjustments are justified only by an observed local gap, never by inventing a missing rail.
+Keep banned KV_SPLIT_DEDUP, KV_SPLIT_EARLY and TF_TP_ROCE_CHUNKED_KB untouched.
+Medium separate proposal: bounded graph-cache ownership/eviction, if this engine's actual graph/program/taps caches demonstrate
+growth; Mia's native-family cache cannot be pasted over this engine's different owners.
+Large proposals:32-row dense replacement, head output-precision change, mHC fusion/overlap arithmetic, new packs,
+or indexer query-row sharding. Each requires its own source/asset ownership, exactness/numeric gates and matched A/B.
